# The Learn application's environment.
#
# The learner application serves many academies from one install, so which
# academy a request is *about* is resolved per request rather than configured
# here. These values say where the API is and how the application presents
# itself.
#
# Nothing here is required: every value has a default that works for a local
# checkout against `pnpm dev`.

# --- Where the API is ---------------------------------------------------------
#
# Read on the server, so it names the API from this process's point of view.
# An origin — scheme, host and port — with no path.
#
# This is also baked into the browser-facing proxy rules at *build* time, because
# Next evaluates `rewrites()` when it loads the config. The browser issues every
# API call against this application's own origin — `/api/v1/...` — and the
# rewrite is what forwards it, which is what keeps the session cookie
# first-party and lets `SameSite=Lax` be enough. A deployment that reaches the
# API somewhere else must set this before building, not only at run time.
API_INTERNAL_URL="http://localhost:4000"

# The same origin, for anything that runs in the browser. Optional: no browser
# code needs an absolute API address, because it goes through the proxy above.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL="http://localhost:4000"

# --- Which academy ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# A self-hosted install on one domain, or one serving several academies from a
# single address, has no per-academy hostname to resolve from. This names the
# academy those requests are about.
#
# It is a deployment value, not a request parameter, so a visitor cannot change
# which academy they are looking at by editing a URL — and it selects what a page
# is *about*, never which academy a caller belongs to. A learner's own academy
# comes from their session row.
NEXT_PUBLIC_ACADEMY_SLUG=""

# --- Images -------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Academy logos live wherever an operator put them, so this cannot be hardcoded.
# Comma-separated hostnames.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_IMAGE_HOSTS="cdn.example.com,images.example.com"

# --- Presentation (optional) --------------------------------------------------
#
# Used for metadata and for the footer's contact link. Both have sensible
# fallbacks, and setting them is cosmetic.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL="https://learn.example.com"
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPPORT_EMAIL="support@example.com"
